\import{algorithms-macros}

\title{\sf{Find} and \sf{Union} run in #{\Theta(\lg n)}}
\date{2026-10-16T21:59:06Z}
\tag{algorithms}
\taxon{Corollary}

\p{\sf{Find} (and hence \sf{Union}) takes time #{\Theta(\lg n)} in the worst case.}

\proof{The worst case is when all #{n} items are contained in a single tree; since any tree of height #{h} must contain at least #{2^h} items, a tree containing #{n} items has a height of at most #{\lg n}.  In the worst case, \sf{Find} takes time proportional to the height of the tree on which it is called (if it starts at a leaf and has to make its way all the way up to the root).}
